---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ConfirmOfficial from "../components/ConfirmOfficial.astro";
import InterestForm from "../components/InterestForm.astro";
---

<Base
  title="The file and the bank"
  description="Andorra residency file checklist: documents, apostilles, medical cover, CASS and opening a bank account."
  path="/the-file"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>The file and the bank</h1>
    <p>
      Most delays are not legal theory. They are a missing apostille, a
      bank that will not take the money, or a medical certificate from
      the wrong clinic.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <ConfirmOfficial />

    <p>
      Build the file as a single pack. Do not send Immigration one
      paper and the bank another story. The same names, dates and
      source-of-wealth have to survive both.
    </p>

    <h2>Papers</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Item</th>
          <th>What usually fails</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Passport</td>
          <td>Expired, or a scan that is not the full booklet they ask for.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Police certificates</td>
          <td>
            Missing apostille or legalisation; wrong country; older than
            the window Immigration will accept.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Housing</td>
          <td>
            A reservation that is not a lease, a title, or another
            accepted certificate.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Means / investment</td>
          <td>
            Numbers that do not match the bank file, or an asset that is
            not yet in a qualifying Andorran form.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Health cover</td>
          <td>
            A tourist policy, or a policy that does not say what
            Immigration is asking for that year.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Medical exam</td>
          <td>The wrong clinic, or a certificate in the wrong form.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Marriage / birth</td>
          <td>Unapostilled, untranslated, or not the current civil status.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Active extras</td>
          <td>
            Company papers, stake, management, CASS, foreign-investment
            authorisation. See
            <a href="/company-active-residency">Company and active residency</a>.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Passive extras</td>
          <td>
            The million, the unit floor if you use property, the AFA
            payment. See
            <a href="/passive-residency">Passive residency in 2026</a>.
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="bank">The bank</h2>
    <p>
      To open a bank account in Andorra you go through Creand, MoraBanc
      or Andbank — and there is a Sabadell presence among them. Mention
      only. We are not adding a new directory listing here. Accounts
      are opened in person. Source-of-wealth is the real interview. The
      account is often a precondition for moving the AFA sum. Resident
      and non-resident products are not the same thing. Do not shop
      four banks with the same thin pack.
    </p>
    <p>
      Andorran Banking’s
      <a
        href="https://www.andorranbanking.ad/en/footer-links/faq/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">FAQ</a
      >
      says accounts cannot be opened directly on the internet, and that
      banks may refuse a customer. Supervision is the
      <a href="https://www.afa.ad/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AFA</a>.
      Official sites we have already sourced are in the
      <a href="/directory">directory</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>CASS</h2>
    <p>
      Active files generally join
      <a href="https://www.cass.ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CASS</a>.
      Employer/employee rates are commonly cited about 15.5% and 6.5%;
      self-employed around 22% of the chosen base. Use current CASS
      tables, not this sentence, for the payment. Passive files do not
      get CASS by working here; they need the private cover Immigration
      asks for.
    </p>

    <h2>Working order</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>#</th>
          <th>Step</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>1</td>
          <td>
            Decide the route. Read
            <a href="/residency-vs-tax">Three things people confuse</a>
            first.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>2</td>
          <td>
            Instruct one gestoria. The shortlist is not filled yet.
            Official sites are in the
            <a href="/directory">directory</a>.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>3</td>
          <td>Collect papers and apostilles. Do this before you book a flight to sign.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>4</td>
          <td>Housing that Immigration will accept, not a screenshot of a listing.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>5</td>
          <td>Bank meeting. Source of wealth. Account in constitution or in your name, as the file needs.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>6</td>
          <td>Medical exam and the cover the permit actually asks for.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>7</td>
          <td>AFA payment, when counsel says the file is ready to take it.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>8</td>
          <td>File at Immigration. Do not invent a date for the card.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>9</td>
          <td>Comú registration, CASS if the route requires it, tax residence as a separate question.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>
      Related:
      <a href="/passive-residency">Passive residency in 2026</a>,
      <a href="/company-active-residency">Company and active residency</a>.
      The
      <a href="/shortlist">private shortlist</a>
      is empty on purpose until a name has been used, checked, or
      explicitly approved. For official websites we have already
      sourced, use the
      <a href="/directory">directory</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <InterestForm
    intro="Leave an email if you want an introduction once a file is actually being prepared. We’ll write back."
    source="the-file"
  />
</Base>
